title: Configuration reference
order: 50
tags: [reference, config]
---

The `quaydoc.toml` file is TOML with three optional tables.

## `[site]`

| key | type | default | meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `title` | string | `Docs` | site title used in `<title>`, feed and footer |
| `base_url` | string | `/` | absolute URL prefix for sitemap and feed links |
| `pretty_urls` | bool | `true` | directory-style URLs with `index.html` |
| `nav_title` | string | site title | short brand shown in the sidebar |
| `toc` | bool | `true` | show the per-page table of contents panel |

## `[build]`

| key | type | default | meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `output_dir` | string | `site` | where rendered pages and assets go |
| `search` | bool | `true` | write `search_index.json` |
| `rss` | bool | `true` | write `feed.xml` |
| `default_lang` | string | `python` | language used for unfenced code |
| `theme` | string | unset | custom theme directory |
| `archive` | string | unset | archive path for `build --archive` |

## `[determ]`

| key | type | default | meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `default_lang` | string | `python` | fallback language for code fences without a label |
| `locale` | string | unset | reserved for future localisation |

## Validation

At build time quaydoc validates types and known keys. Unknown keys are
warnings, not errors, so older trees keep building after upgrades; wrong
types are config errors and stop the build.

## Examples

A minimal tree has no config at all. A realistic configuration:

```toml
[site]
title = "Acme Widget SDK"
base_url = "https://acme.example.net/widget-sdk"
pretty_urls = true

[build]
output_dir = "site"
search = true
rss = false
```
